Module 1: Introduction
Basic components of computer, Execution mechanism of program in computer, Concept of Compiler, Interpreter. Brief of
Machine Language, Assembly Language, and High Level language.

Module 2: Basic Concepts in Programming Paradigms
Problem analysis, Principles and styles of problem-solving, Algorithm, Flow chart, Pseudo code, Syntax, Introduction to Python.

Module 3: Data types and control structures
Data types, variables, expressions, and statements, Operators (unary, arithmetic, etc.), Conditional statement, Assignment
statements, Strings and string operations, Control Structures: loops and decision

Module 4: Function
Defining functions, Functions and arguments (signature), Recursion, Modularization.

Module 5: Array, List, Dictionary
Array, 2D array, Matrix operation, List and Dictionary and their advantages and utility, Tuple and Set.

Module 6: Object oriented concept
Basic concept of object oriented, Class and Object, Difference with structural programming, Object oriented design.

Module 7: Python libraries
NumPy, Basics of NumPy, Various operations on NumPy, Pandas, Basics of Pandas, Reading file using Pandas, DataFrames
creation using Pandas. 

